beware  the spiders we already knew that spiders  were going to be in hogwarts legacy  going off the first trailer when they  appeared for just a brief moment but not  a lot of people have been talking about  this in fact i think some people don't  want to be talking about it hoping that  spiders won't be in the game but i think  that this just about confirms it one of  the big questions among fans are these  acrimantula or a different type of  spider and if they are acromantula does  that break the canon of the original  series so if you're arachnophobe be  prepared don't worry i'm not going to  have any jump scares here but we will be  discussing those furry 8-legged  creatures today now i'll tell you what i  did i pulled out my copy of fantastic  beasts and where to find them no not the  movie the original school book which jk  rowling published all the way back in  2001 with a very large portion of that  going to charity from sales of the book  fantastic beasts and where to find them  of course was written by newt scamander  and represents the fruit of many years  travel and research when newt published  fantastic beasts acromanchiala received  the most severe ministry of magic  classification for magical beasts which  means they're considered known wizard  killers and impossible to train or  domesticate according to the book the  first recorded sighting of an  acromantula came in 1794 so they  definitely would have been around for  the time of hogwarts legacy which is  expected to take place in 1890. now  acromantula originated in borneo and  it's believed they are wizard bread  possibly bread to guard wizard dwellings  or treasure don't forget that bit right  there about guarding wizard dwellings or  treasure we're going to come back to  that another distinct quality of the  acromantula is that they're capable of  human speech yet they aren't self-taught  which indicates their ability to speak  was likely part of a magical breeding  process performed by a witcher wizard i  know totally weird right they're also  considered to be highly intelligent but  remain classified as beasts because  they're incapable of overcoming their  own brutal natures again this is all  according to newt's commander so if  acrimantula originated in borneo and are  bred by wizards would that mean that  aragog was the first acromantula in the  forbidden forest just outside the  hogwarts grounds well let's review his  conversation with harry and ron in  chamber of secrets now of course we all  know after following hagrid's advice to  follow the spiders harry ron and even  fang are captured and taken to aragog  and as they're talking to aragog they  learn a bit about his history here's  what he tells them i was not born in the  castle i come from a distant land a  traveler gave me to hagrid when i was an  egg hagrid was only a boy but he cared  for me hidden in a cupboard in the  castle feeding me on scraps from the  table hagrid is my good friend and a  good man when i was discovered and  blamed for the death of a girl he  protected me i have lived here in the  forest ever since where hagrid still  visits me he even found me a wife mosaic  and you see how our family has grown all  through hagrid's goodness and so from  the information we have there this  doesn't explicitly state that aragog was  the first acromantula in the forbidden  forest what we do know is that it would  appear there were no other females in  the forest at the time because hagrid  had to find him a wife but he also  doesn't make it clear that mosaic was  brought from outside the forest perhaps  mosaic was already there and hagrid  identified her as an ideal mate for  aragog i don't even want to begin  thinking about what hagrid would have  considered for such a thing but hey you  guys know how hagrid he did his own  thing when it came to magical beasts so  personally no i don't think it would  break the canon if acrimantula appear in  the forest in hogwarts legacy that being  said because they aren't native to the  area the story in hogwarts legacy would  definitely need to explain how these  acromantula got to the forest and i  think we already have a perfect  explanation for this with the poachers  that have been confirmed for hogwarts  legacy we've talked many times here  about the role magical creatures are  going to play in this game since the  very first trailer we've seen creatures  in chains wizards wearing animal skull  masks and in the recent autodesk  cutscene we saw a hippogriff being bound  and attacked with spells by a group of  dark wizards now remember that part from  earlier from fantastic beasts that i  said don't forget about the fact that  acromantula were possibly originally  bred to guard wizard dwellings or  treasure we already know one of the big  focuses of hogwarts legacy is going to  be on this so-called ancient magic and  it is my belief that this ancient magic  is not just going to be at hogwarts i  believe there are going to be other  areas outside of hogwarts where we will  be going and finding certain parts of  this ancient magic and one of the places  that you would expect to be a high  probability on that list as a holder of  this ancient magic could very well be  the forbidden force that would make  sense as a place to hide something  incredibly valuable and that brings us  back to the image that avalanche  recently shared beware spiders and it's  clear that having so many here on this  tree it is it's meant as a warning but  there are so many here i mean it almost  seems a little excessive right so was  this put here by the hogwarts staff or  was this actually put up by the group of  poachers as an extra precaution for what  acramantula may be guarding here again  my expectation is they're going to be  guarding one of these strongholds of  ancient magic now thanks to some resumes  from folks that were working on hogwarts  legacy we know there are going to be  various dungeons in the game and three  of those are expected to be referred to  as the castle dungeon goblin dungeon and  cairn dungeon goblin dungeon to me just  screams gringotts right i mean we've  already seen that in the trailer as well  castle dungeon that one's gonna be  somewhere at hogwarts but maybe it's  possible the cairn dungeon could be in  the forest or maybe the forest is  another dungeon entirely now as  terrifying as it will be to traverse  this area and have to take on these  spiders i love the nod to the original  series by including the acromantula here  i think all they need to do is come up  with a clever way of saying that maybe  the poachers brought the acromantula  there or maybe even someone specifically  brought them there just to guard  something but that is not the only nod  to the original series that appears to  be in hogwarts legacy in fact it seems  that we are going to be meeting a couple  of weasleys in this game one of them  possibly even a professor i break that  all down in the video on the right side  of your screen now as always thank you  all so much for watching i'll talk to  you again soon

